From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: report PD-PPS adapter type

Pocket EVO firmware reports USB_TYPE as SDP while USB_ADAP_TYPE correctly
reports PD_PPS (8). The generic usb_type sysfs value therefore cannot be
used as a safe direct-charge preflight.

Track the raw adapter type from a best-effort USB_ADAP_TYPE query and
report POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_PD_PPS only when that query completed with
the raw value 8. Fall back to the existing protocol type otherwise, so
other Qualcomm platforms retain current behavior.

---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -298,6 +298,8 @@
 	unsigned int current_max;
 	unsigned int current_limit;
 	unsigned int usb_type;
+	unsigned int adapter_type;
+	bool adapter_type_valid;
 };
 
 struct qcom_battmgr_wireless {
@@ -1027,6 +1029,12 @@
 
 	mutex_lock(&battmgr->lock);
 	ret = qcom_battmgr_request_property(battmgr, BATTMGR_USB_PROPERTY_GET, prop, 0);
+	/* Best-effort raw adapter query; authoritative for PD-PPS on Pocket EVO. */
+	if (!ret && !qcom_battmgr_request_property(battmgr, BATTMGR_USB_PROPERTY_GET,
+						   USB_ADAP_TYPE, 0))
+		battmgr->usb.adapter_type_valid = true;
+	else
+		battmgr->usb.adapter_type_valid = false;
 	mutex_unlock(&battmgr->lock);
 
 	return ret;
@@ -1070,7 +1078,17 @@
 		val->intval = battmgr->usb.current_limit;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_USB_TYPE:
-		val->intval = battmgr->usb.usb_type;
+		/*
+		 * Pocket EVO firmware reports the protocol type (SDP) on
+		 * USB_TYPE even when the raw USB_ADAP_TYPE read is PD_PPS.
+		 * The adapter read is authoritative for PPS on this machine;
+		 * fall back to the protocol type everywhere else.
+		 */
+		if (battmgr->usb.adapter_type_valid &&
+		    battmgr->usb.adapter_type == 8)
+			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_PD_PPS;
+		else
+			val->intval = battmgr->usb.usb_type;
 		break;
 	default:
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -1634,6 +1652,9 @@
 		case USB_TYPE:
 			battmgr->usb.usb_type = le32_to_cpu(resp->intval.value);
 			break;
+		case USB_ADAP_TYPE:
+			battmgr->usb.adapter_type = le32_to_cpu(resp->intval.value);
+			break;
 		default:
 			dev_warn(battmgr->dev, "unknown property %#x\n", property);
 			break;
